%N A401438 Number of tilings of a strip of length n using squares (length 1) and dominos (length 2), where the total number of tiles is prime.
%H A401438 Leo Zhang, <a href="/A401438/b401438.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..4789</a>
%F A401438 G.f.: A(x) = Sum_{p prime} (x+x^2)^p.
%F A401438 Sum_{p prime, ceiling(n/2) <= p <= n} binomial(p, n-p).
%e A401438 For n=3, we can only have two tiles, which has 3 possible tilings (all squares, domino at index 0 and square at index 2, square at index 0 and domino at index 1).
